## 6. Architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[shared/constants.js] --> B[Express API]
    A --> C[React SPA]
    B -->|Mongoose| D[(MongoDB<br/>Fursad_Platform)]
    B -->|@google/generative-ai| E[Google Gemini]
    B -->|Nodemailer / SMTP| F[Email]
    B <-->|Socket.IO| C
    B --> G[uploads/<br/>CVs and avatars]
```

### Shared constants

`shared/constants.js` holds roles, job statuses, application statuses, language
codes and the matching weights. Both the backend and the frontend import it, so
neither side can drift from the other.

### Backend

- **9 Mongoose models** — User, JobseekerProfile, CV, Company, Job, Application,
  Message, AuditLog, SkillEmbedding
- **49 endpoints** across 8 routers
- **`aiService.js`** — ten Gemini functions, each with a realistic fallback so
  that AI failure never blocks a user
- **`matchingService.js`** — skills 45%, location 20%, salary 15%, education
  10%, experience 10%. The AI extracts and judges; the scoring is deterministic
  arithmetic, which is what makes it explainable
- **`skillMatchService.js`** — semantic skill matching over cached embeddings,
  so `"Node.js"`, `"NodeJS"` and `"Node"` are no longer three different skills
- **`socketHandler.js`** — authenticated real-time chat, scoped per application

### Frontend

- **Three separate auth contexts**, one per portal, with tokens under distinct
  localStorage keys (`fursad_jobseeker_token`, `fursad_provider_token`,
  `fursad_admin_token`) so sessions never collide
- **`services/api.js`** reads `window.location.pathname` and attaches the token
  for whichever portal you are in
- **Route guards** per portal: `JobseekerRoute`, `ProviderRoute`, `AdminRoute`
- **One design system** in `tailwind.config.js` — deep green for structure,
  bright green rationed for actions only, ochre for warmth

