## 7. Things worth knowing

**CVs are personal data.** `backend/uploads/` holds real CVs and profile
photographs. It is git-ignored for that reason, and CVs are never served as
static files — every download goes through an authorised route that checks the
requester actually received that application.

**Rate limits.** Sign-in allows 10 failed attempts per 15 minutes. Anything
that sends an email allows 8 per 10 minutes (`RATE_LIMIT_EMAIL`). Behind a
proxy the app must set `trust proxy`, or every visitor is counted as one.

**A CV is required to apply.** An application with no document attached gives
the employer nothing to read and scores the candidate off an empty profile.

**Run the tests:**

```bash
npm --prefix fursad/backend test
```
